payload.rationale:
The maintainer holds that the ideal is the working folder inside the record's own folder, so mnema stays the centre of the work (ADR-35) and a project has one place for what mnema keeps. ADR-59 put it outside .mnema/, because about ten places treat everything under .mnema/ as signed bytes nobody edits:
- the editorconfig with every property unset, and the attributes;
- the README that forbids hand edits;
- the formatter advice that excludes .mnema/ whole;
- the Action, which skips .mnema/;
- the prose guards;
- the decision-file scan;
- FORMAT section 4, which lists what may sit at the record's root.
The maintainer chose to pay that cost. .mnema/workbench/ is the folder. Its private parts are kept out of git by the record's .gitignore, and the public parts are committed. The record's .editorconfig and attributes are scoped so they no longer reach it. Every place listed above learns that workbench/ is the person's mutable notes and not proof. The readers already enumerate only tails/ and keys/, so verify is unchanged, but FORMAT section 4 gains the folder. That makes it a format-text change, designed with the readers' maintainers' care. What ADR-59 settled otherwise still holds: an init that lays out a skeleton (its shape comes from the architecture study under way), and a brief line naming where the notes are, on by default.

payload.text:
On 22 October 2026 the maintainer questioned whether the workbench should exist at all. mnema today already covers most of what a working folder holds:
- decisions (record_decision);
- traps and lessons (capture_memory);
- measurement results and review findings (record_observation);
- work in flight and what comes next (tasks, next_actions, focus);
- resuming after a pause (resume);
- passing work between sessions (record_handoff);
- the way of working (skills).
What it covers poorly is long text that keeps changing, and evidence files. His direction is to improve mnema on those points and strengthen what makes agents use it, instead of adding a folder. A study maps every kind of working artifact against mnema's current tools before anything is settled. The verb that would create the folder is held unmerged. The record-side change that accepts the folder (#970) stays until the study says whether to keep or revert it.

payload.rationale:
A study mapped every kind of artifact in the maintainer's own working folder (5,614 files, 311 MB) against mnema's current tools. It also counted their use in 93 sessions of this project: 55 record_decision, 23 record_observation and 15 capture_memory calls, but zero create_task, record_handoff, resume, create_skill and bootstrap. Subagents made zero mnema calls across 1,447 transcripts, against 1,486 subagent dispatches. Neither the instruction block nor the server instructions ever name tasks, handoffs, skills or runs.
Decisions, traps, measurements, review verdicts and the way of working already fit the record. Plans, work in flight, handoffs and resuming fit it with small changes. Long text revised many times, evidence files and archives belong outside the record, and mnema points at them by path.
The maintainer settled four things.
(1) No managed folder. The workbench is dropped, the verb in PR 972 is closed, and the record-side change of PR 970 is reverted where it serves only the folder. Kept: the statement that readers enumerate only keys/ and tails/, the inherit.json line, the parity test with unrelated files beside the record, and the reserved name `private`.
(2) Every dispatch of a subagent through the host's Agent tool is mirrored by a hook as a private handoff. It carries the task's short description and the path of a brief when there is one, never the whole prompt, and is on by default (precedent: the host memory mirror).
(3) All of it enters 0.1.3:
- the session journal of ADR-48, with a run's goal and outcome reachable from the MCP, and resume and status printing the outcome;
- a handoff that can carry a brief and a task that can carry a description, both recorded as observations with no format change;
- bootstrap naming a task's owner and last fact;
- refs saying whether a linked path exists and its hash today;
- search finding a decision by its label;
- a line in the instruction block about tasks and handoffs;
- the decision-file hook matching any case.
The A/B of ADR-62 measures whether tasks and handoffs leave zero.
(4) This project's own 0.1.3 work moves into the record now (dogfood): each front a private task, findings as observations, studies and evidence as linked files, so what does not fit shows up as a product gap.

With several projects in one MCP workspace, the first bootstrap or resume opened every other project only to find the agent's last run, and the tool-call count did the same after every call. A derived index of each other project's runs and channel switches cuts that by about 35% (bootstrap 91 to 60 ms with ten projects, measured under load). The first version wrote that index into the other projects' locks/. A review found three problems with that:
- it widens ADR-48, which allowed the read tools a derived cache only in the session's own project;
- an index force-committed into a cloned repository was accepted, so a run's goal could be injected;
- the mark (code stamp, tails extent, sealed segments) served the wrong branch's run after a checkout that swapped the live segment for one of the same size.
The maintainer chose to keep the index under the mnema home, per project and only on this machine. The read tools then write nothing into other projects, ADR-48 stands as written, and an index that arrives with a clone is never read. The mark must also cover the last line of each tail, as the projection file's does, so that a checkout of a same-size segment is seen. An index that fails to parse, or has rows of the wrong shape, is read again from the record and never crashes a tool.

A study weighed Cloudflare's Code Mode for mnema: tools presented as a typed API, and the model writes a short program run in a sandbox. Its main motive, about 11.6k tokens for the 27 tool definitions, looks like an artefact of how the repository measures it. The host contract runs Claude Code 2.1.296 against a stand-in model. Claude Code's documentation says tool search, which defers MCP definitions, is on by default only from v2.1.304. Measured use is isolated writes and almost no reads, the case where code execution helps least. A generic run tool would also take away:
- the honesty sentences in the tool descriptions;
- the readOnlyHint of each tool and the host's approval of each call;
- the mcp_tool hook that calls rules_before_an_edit by name;
- the separation between model code and the process that holds the signing key.
The maintainer chose to measure first and for free: the host contract on Claude Code 2.1.304 or later with tool search on, and what Codex's tool_search returns. A paid trial waits for the 0.1.4 comparison front, and only if the motive survives. It would be a read-only query tool behind a switch, with every write kept as a named tool.
Separately, the idea of a public site for mnema on GitHub Pages, noted on 13 October and never studied, gets its study now and is built in 0.1.4, since 0.1.3's scope is closed.

ADR-53 settled that each repository's own agent rules are written first, as the control arm. The maintainer chose how:
- an agent reads each repository (code, CI, conventions);
- it writes the draft of its CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md on a local branch, with no push;
- the maintainer reviews the drafts and decides what goes in, and who pushes.

The repositories are safeaccess-inline and safeaccess-identum (the safeaccess family) and monitor-sefaz. notagrafo leaves the pilot, which amends the second family of ADR-53.

The control arm (ADR-53, ADR-72) is merged in safeaccess-inline, safeaccess-identum and monitor-sefaz. The maintainer chose to bring the second step into 0.1.3, as a gate beside the A/B:
- the organization's rules, taken from the candidates the control arm listed (the rules shared within the safeaccess family, and the form shared across both families), are drafted locally in felipesauer/.github for him to review, the way the control arm was;
- after his review they are recorded under his own identity and inherited by the three repositories through `mnema inherit`;
- the measurement asks whether a rule decided once in the organization reaches the agent's edit in each repository that inherits it, and is followed, against the copy in each repository's AGENTS.md.

payload.text:
Measured on 26 October 2026, under ADR-73: one session of the maintainer on Sonnet 5.5 (the model of the baseline), on a disposable clone of monitor-sefaz at the baseline commit 61b876e with no remote, against mnema packed from main 689142ba, with the study and scope parts of the baseline prompt. Nothing in the prompt names mnema.
Baseline (0.1.2, 21 October), then this arm (0.1.3):
- calls to mnema's tools: 0, then 10 (bootstrap 1, governing_rules 2, record_decision 4, capture_memory 2, create_task 1), the first at the third tool call;
- decisions recorded: 0, then 4, all 4 with alternatives;
- decisions left only in the study file: 8, then 0;
- memories captured: 0, then 2;
- host notes written: 2, then 0.
The agent asked the scope questions and recorded the three scope decisions after the maintainer answered. It left all four as proposed, for him to accept. The isolation check found no new entry in the real ~/.mnema or ~/.claude.
One session on one model is a count, not a statistic. It also found a defect: mnema status names the private tree's run as the last one and says "1 question answered with no decision recorded after", while the decisions were recorded in the public tree.

payload.rationale:
The maintainer triaged the backlog before the release of 0.1.3.
Four defects found while measuring 0.1.3 go into it before the release:
- mnema status names the private tree's run and says no decision was recorded after a question, when the decisions went to the public tree;
- the required CI checks flake: the loopback-only proof of the Codex and Qwen contracts fails on the Azure runner's DNS, and the Windows drive-letter case fails now and then;
- a CURSOR_VERSION inherited under Qwen Code would run Cursor's write handler too;
- concurrent writes by a new identity all print that they founded it.
Everything else in the backlog goes to 0.1.4:
- all of the hosts and measurement items;
- all of the repository hygiene items;
- the proof and format items, except three that wait for later: Sigstore naming who signs a fact, an attack with a key judged by a verifier a third party writes, and shortening the record's paths for Windows MAX_PATH, which is a format change and his call.
0.1.4 already carried the CLAUDE.md comparison, the GitHub Pages site and the shell coverage study (ADR-68, ADR-69).

payload.text:
Released on 27 October 2026 by the maintainer, through the release workflow and his two approvals:
- the five packages, at 0.1.3 on npm with provenance;
- the tag v0.1.3 and the GitHub release, carrying mnema-0.1.3.vsix;
- the VS Code extension, published as mnema.mnema 0.1.3 to the Visual Studio Marketplace and to Open VSX (ADR-76, ADR-77).
It shipped with the scope ADR-47 set and the decisions that extended it. It was gated by the A/B of ADR-62/73 and by the inheritance pilot of ADR-74/80, whose results are recorded as observations on ADR-62 and ADR-74. The backlog after it was triaged into 0.1.4 (ADR-81).

payload.rationale:
The comparison of ADR-12, ADR-68 and ADR-82 was designed (reference study claude-md-comparison-2026-10). It measures three things separately:
- R: obedience, checked by script;
- D: decisions recorded, and with alternatives;
- Q: recovery of the reason behind a past decision, including a superseded one.
The rules and decisions come from one source and feed both arms, so the arms differ only in where they are carried.
The maintainer chose:
- the pilot size S, ten sessions;
- run interactively, as his own sessions, as the A/B and the inheritance pilot were, with no API key for now;
- a strong CLAUDE.md arm: the rule, its reason, the alternatives turned down, and a line asking the agent to note decisions in the file, so mnema is not measured against a straw man.
The medium and complete sizes, the third arm (CLAUDE.md plus mnema) and headless runs wait for after the pilot.
